From 737a8bb14beafd146db8863eb93abecac1b4cfc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:00:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: block-sparse attention kernels (T5)

Adds minimax_m3_index.cu (index scores + per-128-key block maxima),
minimax_m3_select.cu (forced-block top-16, ascending lists; init/local/tie
rules are launch parameters mirroring minimax_ref.Switches),
minimax_m3_attn.cu (selected-block GQA attention, 16 q heads share one K/V
stream, fixed 32-key steps, decode and prompt) over paged K/V/IK addressed by
page ids (page = 128 tokens). Zig wrapper and std-only geometry module,
kernel registration, gate-5 launch records from nvcc 13.0.88 compiles, GPU
contract test types (compile-checked only), and host tests (geometry, block
boundaries, memory sizing, fp32 host twins vs the float64 reference, planted
mutant controls) as `zig build test-minimax-sparse`. No GPU has run any kernel.
Written from the plan's formulas; no third-party code.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
